# Phase 8: four CPUs report in at boot, and the SMP self-test passes: an
# exact spinlock-protected count from all CPUs, a TLB shootdown that makes a
# reader on another CPU fault at once, work stealing, the heap under all
# CPUs, and no lock-order violation.
smp: cpu 1 online
smp: 4 CPUs online
sched: started on 4 CPU(s)
cerberus kernel shell
!send test smp
!wait 6
4 CPU(s) in use
affinity: a thread pinned to each of 4 CPUs ran on exactly that CPU
spinlock: 4 CPUs x 1000000 increments = 4000000, exact
TLB shootdown: cpu
none got through
work stealing: 8 busy threads ran on 4 different CPUs
heap: 4 CPUs x 40000 allocations
mutex: 4 threads made 200000 increments, none lost
lock order: every spinlock taken above was checked
cleanup:
test smp: PASS
!send test smp
!wait 6
test smp: PASS
!send ps
!wait 2
cpu 3:
